# Zenodo reads .zenodo.json and ignores this file entirely when both are
# present. The two are synchronised by hand: a change to one is a change to
# the other, in the same commit.
#
# The two files carry the same facts in deliberately different notations.
# This is not an inconsistency; do not "correct" one file into the other:
#   licence  .zenodo.json  "cc-by-4.0" (Zenodo's own vocabulary; the SPDX
#                          spelling is not in it)
#            CITATION.cff  CC-BY-4.0   (the SPDX identifier, which CFF
#                          requires)
#                          One value each, and the same one: the licence of
#                          the content. Neither field can carry the code and
#                          document split, and a CFF list would read as OR,
#                          not AND, so it is not used. See REF-003.
#   ORCID    .zenodo.json  bare   0009-0005-5883-1661
#            CITATION.cff  URL    https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5883-1661 (CFF requires it)
#   e-mail   .zenodo.json  has no such field on a creator
#            CITATION.cff  has one, and it is deliberately left out
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  No release has been cited yet. A DOI is minted only when a GitHub Release
  is published from a `cite/` tag.
title: Dactyloscopy
type: software
abstract: >-
  A laboratory for fingerprint research in which every number is traceable to
  the data, the protocol, the metric definition and the code revision that
  produced it.
authors:
  - family-names: Pohuliaiev
    given-names: Yurii
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5883-1661"
    affiliation: "V. N. Karazin Kharkiv National University, Kharkiv, Ukraine"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/matan4life/dactyloscopy"
keywords:
  - fingerprint
  - biometrics
  - reproducibility
  - dactyloscopy
  - minutiae
